---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>
	<h1>Terms & Concepts</h1>

	<h2 class="mt-3">The 3 Main Rules</h2>
	<ul
		class="text-hallebardiers italic leading-[2] gap-5 text-lg glow justify-center"
	>
		<li>Don't get hit</li>
		<li>Hit your opponent</li>
		<li>Make it look good</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 class="mt-8">How to achieve them</h2>
	<div class="mt-3 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
		<article class="card">
			<h3>The 4 states of a duel</h3>
			<p>
				A duel can consist of several states that alternate:
				<span class="italic">Lead, Follow, Reversal and Droid</span>.
				Not all of the states need to occur in a single duel.
			</p>
			<a href="/terms-and-concepts/duel-states"
				>Read more about the duel states</a
			>
		</article>
		<article class="card">
			<h3>The 5 core concepts</h3>
			<p>
				These factors determine how a duel plays out and can both limit
				and inform the actions that can be taken:
				<span class="italic"
					>Technique, Time, Tempo, Opponent, and Terrain</span
				>
			</p>
			<a href="/terms-and-concepts/core-concepts"
				>Read more about the core concepts</a
			>
		</article>
		<article class="card">
			<h3>The Fulchrum</h3>
			<p>
				The imaginary points (multiple!) or line in space that all
				attacks must pass through and you aim to defend always.
			</p>
			<a href="/terms-and-concepts/fulchrum"
				>Read more about the fulchrum</a
			>
		</article>
	</div>
</Layout>
